# Scratch queue rows BLC (plan_process_overhaul.md P2.1). Data: the queue table in scratch_queue.md is generated
# from this file (python3 tools/status_index.py). Format: tools/scratch_query/qrows.py docstring.
# Run: qrun.py run OUT feature_writeup/testing/rows/BLC.qb RES [--section KEY] [--rows ID,...]

@@section 1
@@title Biome tuner disk cache, 2026-10-27
@@phase worldgen
@@date 2026-10-27
@@jars creativecommon creativeworldgen
@@prep A: level-type=minecraft:normal generate-structures=true level-seed=8675309
@@text
@@text Creative Common 1.1.03 (installed 17:25) with the `BiomeLayoutTuner` disk cache and the KubeJS `biome_overrides.js` log
@@text change (TODO server #19, perf.md 11.2 #3). Group A. Fresh world folder; the instance's
@@text `kubejs/generation_scripts/worldgen/biome_layout_cache.json.gz` copied into the scratch server.
@@text
@@table world
## SQ-BLC-01
@group A
@commands Boot a new world; grep latest.log for `[biome-tuning]` and note the time from `biome_overrides.js` to the next KubeJS line
@pass `inputs unchanged, reusing the last solve (disk)`, no `override minecraft:overworld` lines; under 2 s; the world's `level.dat` has the tuned layout (`/locate biome` a tuned rare biome, e.g. one lifted by the rarity floor, finds one as before)
@fails `override ...` lines (a solve): the shipped file's key does not match the jar (seeded from `build/classes`, or jar rebuilt after seeding); re-seed with the jar's classes
@reviewed 2026-11-16
bootexpect \[biome-tuning\] inputs unchanged, reusing the last solve \(disk\)
bootreject \[biome-tuning\] override minecraft:overworld
shell grep -n "biome_overrides\|\[biome-tuning\]" logs/kubejs/server.log logs/latest.log | head -6 | cut -c1-200
> execute positioned 0 70 0 run locate biome minecraft:mushroom_fields
waitlog (nearest minecraft:mushroom_fields|Could not find) 300
look under 2 s between the biome_overrides.js line and the next KubeJS line; the locate finds a rare biome as before
## SQ-BLC-02
@group A
@commands Put a cache file with another key in the server copy (a valid gzip of `{"format":1,"key":"stale"}`), restart; then `/reload`
@pass Boot: the `override` lines (a solve, about 10 s) and the file written again, byte-identical to the instance's copy (`cmp`); `/reload`: `(memory)`
@fails File not written: look for `could not write` in the messages; differs: the solve is not deterministic
@reviewed 2026-11-26
# 2026-11-26 (writer-3, r1120nv judge-9): deleting the server copy no longer forces a solve: WorldgenFiles.existing falls back to the
# creativeworldgen jar's copy of the file ("reusing the last solve (disk)"), and the write is skipped when the text equals the jar's
# copy. A cache file with another key is read as "other key: solve" (BiomeLayoutTuner.readDiskCache) and is rewritten (its text differs).
edit mkdir -p kubejs/generation_scripts/worldgen && printf '{"format":1,"key":"stale"}' | gzip -n > kubejs/generation_scripts/worldgen/biome_layout_cache.json.gz && test -s kubejs/generation_scripts/worldgen/biome_layout_cache.json.gz
restart
bootexpect \[biome-tuning\] override minecraft:overworld
bootreject \[biome-tuning\] inputs unchanged, reusing the last solve \(disk\)
bootreject could not write
shell test -s kubejs/generation_scripts/worldgen/biome_layout_cache.json.gz && cmp kubejs/generation_scripts/worldgen/biome_layout_cache.json.gz "$INST/kubejs/generation_scripts/worldgen/biome_layout_cache.json.gz" && echo "cache rewritten, identical"
> reload
waitlog \[biome-tuning\] inputs unchanged, reusing the last solve \(memory\) 120
look the solve on the boot took about 10 s (override lines), the rewritten file is byte-identical to the shipped one

## SQ-BLC-03
@group A
@commands Change one biome multiplier in `biome_config.json` (badlands 1 -> 1.5), boot; restore it, boot; boot again
@pass A solve with the new value and the file rewritten with a new key; restore the value, boot: solve again (the file holds the shipped key again), then `(disk)` on the boot after
@fails `(disk)` right after the edit: the key misses the config
@reviewed 2026-11-26
# 2026-11-26 (writer-3): three boots in one row; the edits run in OUT/srv while the server is down. The config is copied from the
# instance first so the edit has a file to change (the pack's kubejs may not be in srv).
edit mkdir -p kubejs/generation_scripts/worldgen && cp -f "$INST/kubejs/generation_scripts/worldgen/biome_config.json" kubejs/generation_scripts/worldgen/biome_config.json && python3 -c "import json,sys; p='kubejs/generation_scripts/worldgen/biome_config.json'; d=json.load(open(p)); d['dimensions']['minecraft:overworld']['biomes']['minecraft:badlands']['multiplier']=1.5; json.dump(d,open(p,'w'),indent=2)"
restart
bootexpect \[biome-tuning\] override minecraft:overworld
bootreject \[biome-tuning\] inputs unchanged, reusing the last solve \(disk\)
shell zcat kubejs/generation_scripts/worldgen/biome_layout_cache.json.gz | python3 -c "import json,sys; print(json.load(sys.stdin)['key'])" > .blc3_key1 && test -s .blc3_key1
edit cp -f "$INST/kubejs/generation_scripts/worldgen/biome_config.json" kubejs/generation_scripts/worldgen/biome_config.json
restart
bootexpect \[biome-tuning\] override minecraft:overworld
bootreject \[biome-tuning\] inputs unchanged, reusing the last solve \(disk\)
shell zcat kubejs/generation_scripts/worldgen/biome_layout_cache.json.gz | python3 -c "import json,sys; print(json.load(sys.stdin)['key'])" > .blc3_key2 && test -s .blc3_key2 && ! cmp -s .blc3_key1 .blc3_key2 && zcat "$INST/kubejs/generation_scripts/worldgen/biome_layout_cache.json.gz" | python3 -c "import json,sys; print(json.load(sys.stdin)['key'])" | cmp .blc3_key2 - && echo "key changed with the edit, back to the shipped key after the restore"
restart
bootexpect \[biome-tuning\] inputs unchanged, reusing the last solve \(disk\)
bootreject \[biome-tuning\] override minecraft:overworld
@@text
@@text Results 2026-10-27 night: SQ-BLC-01 PASS (`(disk)` on every boot with the shipped file, 1.4 s; `/reload` `(memory)`); tuned-biome locate not run. SQ-BLC-02 PASS: file deleted -> solve (14.7 s) and the rewritten file byte-identical to the instance copy. SQ-BLC-03 PASS: badlands multiplier 1 -> 1.5 solved (13.6 s) and rewrote the file; restoring it solved again (combined with -02).
